pick_failed.prompt:
The pick failed (exit {{exit_code}}):
{{stdout}}
{{stderr}}
A held lock (`<queue>.lock`: another pick is writing) → `retry`. A malformed queue (not YAML, no
`batch_size:`, a bad task) → fix the header and `retry`, or `stop`.

work_unverified.prompt:
The worker's result of {{context.task}} is not on the tree (exit {{exit_code}}):
{{stdout}}
{{stderr}}
The worker did not leave one clean commit on its branch: `fix` sends it the cause — the lines above, and
its report.md / handoff.md — as another round of `work`; `blocked` when it is stuck or another round
would not help.

cleanup_failed.prompt:
Bookkeeping or cleanup of the landed {{context.task}} refused (exit {{exit_code}}):
{{stdout}}
{{stderr}}
Leave what it kept; make sure the task is done (`queue_mark` to `done` if the mark step failed) and
note what was kept on it. Transition `done`.

stopped.prompt:
Task {{context.task}} STOPPED: report to the user the task, the reason, and the exact state of
{{context.cwd}}:
{{context.repo_state}}
A driver: put that in a NEEDS-PARENT line and
stop — the dispatcher's session is not yours. The dispatcher itself (no driver): in {{parent_session_id}}
transition `stop`.
